                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Almost certain this is not possible. Isn't `NaN` a float/double value?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Fan.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Joseph-Jonathan Salzano",
                        "email": "joseph-jonathan.salzano@hp.com",
                        "username": "jsalzano92"
                    },
                    "message": "I was currious about this. What would be the right \"default\" to show that the MaxRatedRPM is unknown? We use 0 at HP, but not sure what OpenBMC would like to see as a whole."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Fan.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "0 seems reasonable.  The alternative is `maxint`.\n\nWhatever you have as the default here you'll need code in bmcweb to recognize this and treat is as null."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Fan.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Joseph-Jonathan Salzano",
                        "email": "joseph-jonathan.salzano@hp.com",
                        "username": "jsalzano92"
                    },
                    "message": "right that was the next step, if others feel like 0 is reasonable that is what I would use, easy to check against in bmcweb too. I'll make the change."
                }
            ],
